{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43821 - PROTEIN:4892",
  "verbalization": "Octadecanenitrile is implicated in the targeting of CD70 antigen through a multi-step pathway. The evidence suggests that Octadecanenitrile directly interacts with DMS-79, which in turn is targeted by 7,10-Octadecadienoic acid, methyl ester, and by Cinnamtannin A2. Both of these compounds ultimately lead to the activation of CD70 antigen. The high scores in all three paths indicate a consistent and robust relationship, suggesting that Octadecanenitrile may act as a modulator or activator of the signaling cascade that leads to CD70 expression. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Octadecanenitrile influences the expression of CD70 antigen through the regulation of downstream targets, possibly by modulating the activity of the 7,10-Octadecadienoic acid, methyl ester, or Cinnamtannin A2 pathways. This suggests that Octadecanenitrile may play a role in the biological process of CD70 antigen upregulation, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism.",
